africa's billionaires are richer than  they've been in years despite the global  pandemic  as a group the continent's 18  billionaires are worth an estimated 84.9  billion dollars a 15 increase from 12  months ago  soaring stock prices lifted the fortunes  of these tycoons as demands for products  from cement to luxury goods ticked up  for the 11th year in a row aliko dangote  of nigeria is the continent's richest  person worth an estimated 13.9 billion  dollars up from 12.1 billion dollars  last year following a 30 increase in the  stock price of dengote cement his most  valuable asset  analysts found a surge in housing  developments in nigeria and growth in  government infrastructure spending drove  higher demand for cement in the first  nine months of 2021. jumping into the  number two spot up for number four last  year is luxury goods magnate johann  rupert of south africa shares of his  company financiary richmond maker of  cartier watches in mont blanc pens  surged more than 60 and pushed his  fortune to 11 billion dollars up from  7.2 billion dollars a year ago making  him the biggest dollar gainer on the  list south african nikki oppenheimer who  formerly ran diamond mining firm to  beers before selling it to mining firm  anglo-american a decade ago ranks number  three worth an estimated 8.7 billion  dollars  the biggest gainer in percentage terms  is drive masayuwa of zimbabwe worth 2.7  billion dollars up from 1.2 billion  dollars last year a 125 increase  shares of econet wireless zimbabwe which  he founded rose more than 750 in the  past year helping to drive up the size  of his fortune the 18 billionaires from  africa hail from seven different  countries south africa and egypt each  have five billionaires followed by  nigeria with three in morocco with two  all of the continent's billionaires are  men the last woman to appear in the  ranks isabel dos santos of angola fell  off the forbes list in january 2021  [Music]  you
 

